      "headline": "Manufacturing employment edges up 0.1% in June after four monthly declines",
      "context": "The increase ended a four-month slide, but factory employment remained below a year earlier for a 40th consecutive month. Computer-equipment manufacturing was the exception.",
      "background": "The Mexican statistics agency's manufacturing survey tracks payroll employment across the factory sector. A 0.1% monthly rise shows that June was better than May, but it does not erase 40 straight months of year-over-year declines.",
      "view": "The split matters more than the small monthly gain. Factory hiring is still weak across the sector, while computer equipment is growing with demand for data-center hardware. That is a narrow pocket of strength, not a broad manufacturing recovery.",
      "prediction": "Watch the July survey for another monthly increase and fewer year-over-year losses across industries. If computer equipment remains the main exception, the recovery is still narrow.",
      "analysisV": 9,
