      "headline": "Mexico's aviation regulator says FAA review results are due within 60 days",
      "context": "AFAC said it answered all questions in the review and that the FAA thanked it for providing the requested information. The US regulator has not announced a result.",
      "background": "The FAA restored Mexico to Category 1 in September 2023. That status lets Mexican airlines add US routes and codeshares. The latest review tests whether Mexico's regulator still meets international safety-oversight standards.",
      "view": "The on-site review is finished, but the safety finding is not. Mexico remains Category 1 while it waits. The business risk begins only if the FAA finds that oversight has slipped and changes the rating.",
      "prediction": "Watch the FAA's country-rating list or a formal notice by mid-October. Category 1 staying in place would confirm continued compliance. A downgrade would again limit new US routes and codeshares.",
